# R14 — decompose the recipe. Chapter 4 §4.5 says "the recipe as a whole determines how
# circular the solution is", which is an admission rather than a finding: the two headline
# regimes differ in six things at once, and the weight-decay dose sweep already showed the
# dose alone is not it.
#
# The six, measured from the two manifests rather than assumed:
#
#   factor          reference (p=113, wd 0.1)   canonical (p=97, wd 1.0)
#   batch size      512                          full batch
#   learning rate   3e-3                         1e-3
#   depth           2 blocks                     1 block
#   activation      GELU                         ReLU
#   MLP width       256                          512
#   Adam epsilon    1e-6                         1e-8
#
# Modulus and weight decay are held at the reference regime's values (p=113, wd 0.1), so
# the dose confound is removed by construction and every cell differs from an anchor in
# exactly one factor. Two anchors, six single-factor flips from each, three seeds: 42 runs
# on a uniform 200k budget, because a comparison across cells cannot also vary the budget.
#
# run_name is explicit: the default interpolation encodes none of these six, so all
# fourteen cells would collide with each other and with the existing reference runs.

# --- from the reference anchor ---
+experiment=tang_repro run_name=transformer_add113_f0.3_wd0.1_recipe-rT_s0 seed=0 train.steps=200000 train.snapshot_schedule=linear train.n_snapshots=120 train.metric_every=500 train.capture_representations=false
